{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1024536-diablerizing-a-beast-the-primordial","id":1024536,"title":"Diablerizing a Beast (the Primordial)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-30T16:11:27-08:00","id":1024536,"title":"Diablerizing a Beast (the Primordial)","content":"This unusual situation came up as a result of my the last session of my VtR game. The game I'm running primarily focuses on Kindred, but there was a singular Beast (as in, Beast the Primordial) who served as a secondary antagonist largely focused on keeping the vampire population hemmed into a fairly small downtown area. So in a previous session two of my player characters came across the Beast in a park and angered her by not showing her the fear and respect that she demands from the Kindred population. She decided to try and put some fear into them and began imposing her Lair on the world, prompting them to defend themselves. The Nosferatu character used his Nightmare discipline, prompting the Beast to become terrified and run away, a humiliating act that fostered a powerful need for revenge in her. So, naturally, being a vindictive, petty Beast, she decided to invade the Nosferatu's haven, attempt to murder his Touchstone, then arrange for him to come across it and feed off of his terror.<br /> <br /> Things didn't go as said Beast planned. She failed to completely kill the Touchstone, and the Nosferatu managed to get a hold of her and sink his fangs in. Knowing that the Beast would keep coming back and attack his loved ones again and again, the Nosferatu used everything he had to take her down, and he managed to kill her by draining every ounce of blood in her body. Seeing as how this is basically the same manner in which a Kindred commits Diablerie, I talked with my group and we all decided that it seems like it'd be great if the amount of supernatural blood the Nosferatu imbibed caused some kind of permanent change in him. Fueling this idea is how oddly similar these two characters are on a thematic level. Both are creatures that utilize Nightmare fear-based powers, both are fairly weak physically but seek to create the illusion of extreme danger to keep enemies at bay, and both utilize shadows as their aesthetic theme (the Beast sinks into and teleports through shadows, watching people from within them, the Nosferatu's curse takes the form of shifting, whispering shadows swirling around him).<br /> <br /> Currently I'm a bit paralyzed as to what to give him, simply because there are so many possibilities, so I thought I'd see if anyone had any cool ideas. I'd like the boon to be fairly substantial (the Beast was of a greatly higher power than the Nosferatu), but I'd like it to also have a significant downside as well, perhaps a new bane. The Beast killed was an Eshmaki Nemesis with Lair 3 and lair traits of Darkness, Silence, and Maze. She utilized the atavisms Eye of Heaven, Shadowed Soul, and From the Shadows and the nightmares You Deserve This and Behold My True Form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:16:49-08:00","id":1024541,"title":"","content":"Oh, dude, have her blood act as the blood of an Avus and let him join the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">Khaibit Bloodline</a>! (Ignoring the usual Clan restriction, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-30-2016, 07:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:23:45-08:00","id":1024545,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a cool game. I sometimes use ideas from Masquerade Disciplines for this kind of thing. Charlaquin has it right, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-shadow-and-the-asp/\" target=\"_blank\">the Khaibit powers have sort of been ported over via official writer, so you have the mechanics</a>. I might suggest something more akin to the Lygos bloodline, but with the Khaibit's Obtenebration. Though considering the differences in viewpoints, Khaibit does make more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:29:39-08:00","id":1024547,"title":"","content":"<b>The Boon</b><br /> Consuming the Beast gives the Nosferatu insight into its own nature. The Nosferatu gains &quot;You Deserve This&quot; as a special Nightmare Devotion (Substitute Blood Potency+Nightmare for Satiety where needed - the Devotion does not have the Satiety Expenditure option).<br /> <br /> <b>The Flaw</b><br /> The Vampire Triggers Hero's and appears as a Beast to powers capable of detecting them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:31:09-08:00","id":1024548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1024536-diablerizing-a-beast-the-primordial?p=1024547#post1024547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Boon</b><br /> Consuming the Beast gives the Nosferatu insight into its own nature. The Nosferatu gains &amp;quot;You Deserve This&amp;quot; as a special Nightmare Devotion (Substitute Blood Potency+Nightmare for Satiety where needed - the Devotion does not have the Satiety Expenditure option).<br /> <br /> <b>The Flaw</b><br /> The Vampire Triggers Hero's and appears as a Beast to powers capable of detecting them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's way better than my idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T16:32:40-08:00","id":1024550,"title":"","content":"A Flaw could be that the Beast (as in the Nosferatu's Beast) has inherited the Beast character's Hunger along with that for blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T21:40:11-08:00","id":1024628,"title":"","content":"It's been a very fun game. This is me and everyone else in the group's first experience with VtR, and it's really the furthest I've ever come to running a straight sandbox style game too.<br /> That Khaibit bloodline looks really appropriate on the surface but I'm not sure it's a great fit. The first dot it grants isn't really that useful (vampire's can already see in very low light) and all the other dots require a lot of prerequisite disciplines that would take a very long time for him to develop. I do like the idea of a unique bloodline though. I was thinking of having the drawback be some kind of new bane involving an aversion to bright light. Like ordinary bright lighting (like you'd get in a Walmart or something) would be uncomfortable and maybe give some penalties to certain dicepools (perception, resolve + composure rolls, etc.) while extreme bright lights (like floodlights) would be capable of bashing damage. Ideally it would accompany some power that makes him more capable in darkness.<br /> <br /> Has anyone else had something of this sort come up in a game before? Vampires drinking from other supernatural creatures and gaining some effect or condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T22:01:23-08:00","id":1024632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluespade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1024536-diablerizing-a-beast-the-primordial?p=1024628#post1024628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone else had something of this sort come up in a game before? Vampires drinking from other supernatural creatures and gaining some effect or condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>First edition had a variety of effects for just drinking the blood of other supernaturals. Diablerie is a bit different, and I think it only came up with vampires, humans and ghosts, the latter in bloodlines.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing about this case is that diablerie is the devouring of a soul. But a Beast doesn't have a soul, it has a Soul, made of a Horror. The vampire would have ingested an entity born of fear and fright. And while it's easy to say nothing happened, it's fun to have something cool as a result of this likely once in an unlifetime act. Since a vampire gains Disciplines or Skills from those they commit diablerie on, perhaps they gain one of the Beast's Nightmares, as Reighnhell said. I like the idea of it becoming the Avus of a bloodline and perhaps gaining the powers of the Khaibit because you said the Beast was linked with Darkness, Silence and Maze. The first one is a big thing to Khaibit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T22:57:38-08:00","id":1024640,"title":"","content":"Though a great suggestion with gifting a Nightmare to the player has been made, I'd give the player a merit that grants them something akin to the Beast's lair traits - not imposing them, but becoming immune or at least gaining a resistance to them. Darkness would become more dim than a true shade, mazes would confer an innate logic, and silence wouldn't be absolute, simply dim.<br /> <br /> Then again I just thought of that off the top of my head, so I dunno how well that would work in the long run. Cool situation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T01:42:36-08:00","id":1024670,"title":"","content":"Maybe hint and allude that diablerizing more Beasts will gift further powers, thus giving the vampire a damn good motive to start hunting Beasts. Good justification for why you would hold out on giving all those shiny new powers at once, and a good story hook potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T09:46:53-08:00","id":1024793,"title":"","content":"I should probably mention that it's been hinted that one of the other player's Touchstones, his sister, is a latent Beast who hasn't been awoken yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12090-bluespade","name":"Bluespade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T06:44:33-08:00","id":1027598,"title":"","content":"Give the Vampire the Beasts lair, which he can travel to simularily to how the beast did, but at the price that he hears the screams, roars, ect... Of the Beasts horror at all times, endlessly, pushing to him towards feeding reckless and often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T07:39:13-08:00","id":1027641,"title":"","content":"Creating a custom bloodline is almost definitely the way to go, even if its an add-hoc bloodline.<br /> <br /> One potential avenue would be let the nosferatu impose lair traits (NEVER traits that interact with banes like fire or sunlight). In this case, give the bloodline a custom discipline loosely based off of how a beast's Lair trait works. The bloodline weakness should be that you can only gain nourishment from people who have just experienced a breaking point or are inside the lair. Have The Beast (vampire's beast) be what lurks in the lair.<br /> <br /> Offhand, for the discipline.<br /> Dot 1 lets you collect up to 1+(Discipline) Chambers. First one is your Heart, the rest must be collected. Your Beast lurks here in perpetual frenzy, wuth a spirit form like a beast's (no bonus traits).<br /> Dot 2 You may impose Lair Traits on the world like a beast. You may impose one, but hold up to (Discipline).<br /> Dot 3 You may bring your Lair to the real world and trap people there like a Beast can. Merge with your Beast when in your lair.<br /> Dot 4 Basically primordial pathways + hold the gate.<br /> Dot 5 You can diablerize spaces.<br /> <br /> +1 for a bonus Nightmare and a weakness. Attracting heroes may be too much.<br /> <br /> Though it seems like you more want something geared to Shadows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:18:57-08:00","id":1027743,"title":"","content":"There have been a lot of great suggestions here, but I have noticed that no one is treating it like diablerie. Giving you a new bloodline is actually the one thing that diablerie can't give you ( a bloodline discipline ) you could for sure have your vampire get to BP 6 and create a new bloodline with the beast heavily wrapped into it. But as Raw you have to be BP 6 to create a new bloodline. Which is an awesome idea.<br /> <br /> Also draining something completely of it's blood is not diablerie. Diablerie has it's own rolls and you actually have to want to swallow it's soul.<br /> <br /> I have a serial diablerist who has eaten Werewolves and a Changeling ( and many many vampires ) But what the ST did, is that she treated it just like diablerie.<br /> <br /> 1 dot of discipline equivalent. So for the werewolves she gave me gifts according to their Moons. and BP EXP to spend on their Primal power, the BP equivalent trait.<br /> For the changeling she gave me BP EXP based on the Wyrd and she gave me ermm... I don't remember the changeling titles. Contract power?<br /> <br /> <br /> When I did get my vampire to BP 8 I ended up creating a bloodline around the diablerie and merging in the other races into it. It kind of turned out pretty neat.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Dont forget: the Diablerie addiction and all that fun stuff!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 01-06-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}